<div class="pathway-content">
  <h1 class="page-header">Age of Abandonment</h1>

  <div class="exhibit-text">
    <p class="poem-title">One-Way Ticket</p>

    <p>Subida a otro avi&oacute;n de American Airlines<br>
    que empieza a descender hacia la isla<br>
    siento<br>
    luces en el mar.</p>

    <p>De espaldas a la realidad<br>
    parece tan f&aacute;cil y tan simple.</p>
  </div>

  <img class="boardingpass align-right" src="{{ '/assets/images/path-predictable-precarity/onewayticket-boarding-pass.jpg' | url }}" alt="Nicole Delgado's boarding pass back to Puerto Rico">

  <div class="exhibit-text clear-right">
    <p class="poem-title">Las casas vac&iacute;as</p>

    <p>Al cabo de un tiempo de regreso<br>
    No te escapas de pensar en la renta versus la loza criolla,<br>
    La pintura con plomo versus los balustres de cemento<br>
    Y la luz a trav&eacute;s de los bloques ornamentales.</p>

    <p>No te escapes de admirar los medios puntos<br>
    De las casas vac&iacute;as que se dejan perder en cada calle.<br>
    Estas casas vac&iacute;as con las ventanas tapiadas,<br>
    Estorbos p&uacute;blicos le dice,<br>
    A las casas de los muertos con los hijos en Estados Unidos.</p>

    <p>No, t&uacute; no te escapas.</p>

    <p>T&uacute; que has regresado de vivir en los Estados Unidos<br>
    No te escapas del deseo de abrir y de habitar sin pagar renta<br>
    Esas casas viejas y vac&iacute;as.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="curator-msg float-right">
    <p>Hurricane Mar&iacute;a accelerated a pattern of migration of Puerto Ricans to the U.S. mainland that had been on the rise since the island&rsquo;s fiscal crisis exploded around 2010. Many artists and scholars have sought to express the experiences of those displaced. Others have focused on what has been left behind, declaring a new &ldquo;age of abandonment&rdquo; of Puerto Rico in the twenty-first century. Bucking this trend, the poet Nicole Delgado returned to the island permanently in 2012. From the collection <em>Periodo Especial</em>, her poems &ldquo;One Way Ticket&rdquo; and &ldquo;Las casas vac&iacute;as&rdquo; reflect upon the moments of grace and hardship inherent in returning to and living in landscapes others have abandoned.</p>

    <p>Learn more about <a class="link" href="{{ '/people/#ndelgado' | url }}">Nicole Delgado and La Impresora</a>.</p>
  </div>

